---
---

<section id="features" class="section">
  <div class="container-tool">
    <div class="text-center max-w-2xl mx-auto mb-10">
      <p class="eyebrow">Everything you need</p>
      <h2 class="h-section mt-3">A complete YAML toolset</h2>
      <p class="lead mt-4">Format, validate, convert, visualize, and verify — all in one browser-based toolkit.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-5">
      {[
        { icon: 'M4 6h16M4 12h16M4 18h16', title: 'Instant Formatting', desc: 'Beautify messy YAML with perfect, consistent indentation in milliseconds. The formatter normalizes spacing and aligns nesting, turning unreadable configs into clean, scannable files — whether you have two lines or two thousand.' },
        { icon: 'M9 12l2 2 4-4m6 2a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z', title: 'Syntax Validation', desc: 'Every input is checked against the YAML 1.2 specification. Errors are highlighted with the exact line and column, plus a plain-language hint explaining what went wrong and how to fix it — no more guessing which line broke your deploy.' },
        { icon: 'M14.5 2H6a2 2 0 00-2 2v16a2 2 0 002 2h12a2 2 0 002-2V7.5L14.5 2z', title: 'File Upload & Drag', desc: 'Drop .yaml or .yml files straight into the editor, or paste from anywhere. Everything runs locally in your browser, so sensitive keys and credentials never leave your machine.' },
        { icon: 'M7 16V4m0 0L3 8m4-4l4 4m6 0v12m0 0l4-4m-4 4l-4-4', title: 'YAML to JSON, TOML & XML', desc: 'Convert YAML to JSON, TOML, or XML in one click. The conversion is lossless and follows YAML 1.2, so nested objects, arrays, anchors, and aliases all resolve correctly — perfect for feeding configs into APIs, CI tools, and JSON-, TOML-, or XML-only pipelines.' },
        { icon: 'M12 3v1m0 16v1m9-9h-1M4 12H3m15.364 6.364l-.707-.707M6.343 6.343l-.707-.707m12.728 0l-.707.707M6.343 17.657l-.707.707M16 12a4 4 0 11-8 0 4 4 0 018 0z', title: 'Real-time Feedback', desc: 'See the formatted output update as you type — no submit button, no waiting. The instant feedback loop lets you experiment with indentation and structure until everything reads exactly right.' },
        { icon: 'M13 10V3L4 14h7v7l9-11h-7z', title: 'Multi-document', desc: 'YAML files often hold several documents separated by ---, like a Deployment plus a Service. The formatter processes each document independently and preserves the separators, so nothing gets merged or lost.' },
        { icon: 'M12 22s8-4 8-10V5l-8-3-8 3v7c0 6 8 10 8 10z', title: 'JSON Schema Validation', desc: 'Validate your YAML against a JSON Schema to catch structural errors — wrong field names, missing required keys, invalid types — before they break a deployment. A capability most other YAML tools do not offer.' },
        { icon: 'M12 3v2m0 0v15m0-15l-5 6m5-6l5 6M4 21h16', title: 'Tree View', desc: 'Visualize any YAML document as a collapsible tree with values color-coded by type. It\'s the fastest way to understand deeply nested configs and confirm every key ended up where you intended.' },
        { icon: 'M8 3H5a2 2 0 00-2 2v3m18 0V5a2 2 0 00-2-2h-3m0 18h3a2 2 0 002-2v-3M3 16v3a2 2 0 002 2h3', title: 'Expand Anchors', desc: 'Resolve YAML anchors (&), aliases (*), and merge keys (<<) into fully expanded values with one checkbox. Instantly see the final structure your tooling actually receives — no more tracing references by hand.' },
      ].map(({ icon, title, desc }) => (
        <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl border border-zinc-200 bg-white">
          <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-blue-50 flex items-center justify-center mb-4">
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-blue-600" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d={icon}/></svg>
          </div>
          <h3 class="h-sub">{title}</h3>
          <p class="mt-1.5 text-sm text-zinc-500 leading-relaxed">{desc}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
